# macOS
.DS_Store

# CPM transient session-state files (created/deleted by running skills)
# All three are per-session scratch keyed by CPM_SESSION_ID. Only the progress file
# was ignored, so summaries and cleancheck markers from dead sessions accumulated in
# git — three of them were committed before this was noticed.
docs/plans/.cpm-progress-*.md
docs/plans/.cpm-compact-summary-*.md
docs/plans/.cpm-cleancheck-*

# dpm's generated database (AD4). `.dpm/dpm.sql` is the committed form and is NOT ignored;
# `.dpm/dpm.db` is built from it and is machine-local. Added when Epic 47-03 Story 2 wired the
# tool registry to the entry point, which is the point at which launching the server anywhere
# in this tree started producing the file.
.dpm/dpm.db

# The ralph loop's own state, rewritten on every iteration. An unattended run commits after
# each story and stages everything, so without this line the loop's iteration counter lands in
# the work's commits. The run's memory is a dpm session row, not this file.
.claude/ralph-loop.local.md
